{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>The voice is the voice of Jacob.</b> They said in the Midrash: Jacob has dominion only through his voice, as it is said, ״הקול קול יעקב״, and Esau has dominion only through his hands, as it is said, ״והידים ידי עשו״; and so it says (Psalms 20) ״אלה ברכב ואלה בסוסים ואנחנו בשם ה׳ אלהינו נזכיר״, and likewise Moses said to the king of Edom (Numbers 20) ״ונצעק אל ה׳ וישמע קולנו״. R. Abbahu bar Kahana said: No philosophers arose in the world like Balaam son of Beor and Avnimus the Gardianite. All the nations of the world came to him; they said to him: Do you believe that we can match ourselves against this nation? He said to them: Go and make the rounds of their synagogues and study halls — if you find children chirping with their voices, you cannot overcome them, and if not, you can overcome them, for thus did their father promise them: ״הקול קול יעקב״ — when Jacob's voice is present in synagogues and study halls, ״אין הידים ידי עשו״ — the hands are not the hands of Esau."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {0 "Citations to Psalms 20 and Numbers 20 written without verse numbers in the source; the quoted phrases correspond to Psalms 20:8 and Numbers 20:16-17. The name אבנימוס הגרדי transliterated; likely referring to Oenomaus of Gadara."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:15:37.475500460Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}